.TH PDFCANCEL 1 "November 2026" "pdfcancel 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdfcancel \- Convert PDF documents to clean markdown using AI-powered OCR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfcancel
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]

.B pdfcancel
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIPDF_FILE\fR

.B pdfcancel backlog
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIDIRECTORY\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfcancel
is a command-line tool that converts PDF documents to clean, readable
markdown format using AI-powered Optical Character Recognition (OCR).
It supports both Mistral AI's native OCR service and any OpenAI-compatible
vision model, making it versatile for cloud-based or local/self-hosted
OCR workflows.

The tool excels at handling complex PDFs including those with:
.IP "\fB\-\fR" 4
Scanned documents
.IP "\fB\-\fR" 4
Multi-column layouts
.IP "\fB\-\fR" 4
Tables and figures
.IP "\fB\-\fR" 4
Mathematical notation
.IP "\fB\-\fR" 4
Images and diagrams (with --full)

.SH OCR ENGINES
.TP
.B mistral (default)
Uses Mistral AI's native OCR API (model: mistral-ocr-latest).
Requires the MISTRAL_API_KEY environment variable.
Best for general-purpose PDF conversion with high accuracy.

.TP
.B vlm
Uses any OpenAI-compatible vision model via the /v1/chat/completions
endpoint. Supports local inference with Ollama, vLLM, LiteLLM, or any
OpenAI-compatible server. Activate with --ocr-engine vlm or by setting
--api-base.

.SH COMMON OPTIONS
For the default convert command (applied to single PDFs or when invoked
directly with a PDF path):

.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Output directory for converted files. Default: same directory as input PDF.

.TP
.B \-\-images
Extract figures and images from the PDF to a companion directory named
<input>_images/. Images are referenced in the markdown output.

.TP
.B \-\-embed-images
Embed all images as base64-encoded data URIs directly in the markdown
output instead of using external file references.

.TP
.B \-\-plaintext
Output plain text instead of markdown. Disables all markdown formatting.

.TP
.B \-\-full
Full multimodal conversion. In addition to text extraction, AI-describes
all charts, figures, diagrams, and images using a vision model.
Requires a vision-capable model. Implies --images.

.TP
.B \-\-full-model \fIMODEL\fR
Vision model to use for --full image descriptions. Default:
pixtral-large-latest. For vlm engine: any vision model supported by your
endpoint (e.g., llava, gemma-4-vision). For mistral engine: multimodal
model name.

.TP
.B \-\-ocr-engine \fIENGINE\fR
OCR engine to use: 'mistral' (default) or 'vlm'.

.TP
.B \-\-api-base \fIURL\fR
OpenAI-compatible server URL for vlm engine. Examples:
http://localhost:11434 (Ollama), http://localhost:8000/v1 (vLLM).
Implicitly sets --ocr-engine to vlm.

.TP
.B \-\-api-key \fIKEY\fR
Bearer token for vlm endpoint authentication. Not needed for local
Ollama. Overrides PDFCANCEL_API_KEY environment variable.

.TP
.B \-\-ca-bundle \fIPATH\fR
CA bundle (PEM file) to verify self-hosted server's TLS certificate.
Required for HTTPS endpoints with self-signed certificates.

.TP
.B \-\-model \fIMODEL\fR
Model override for the active engine. For mistral: OCR model name.
For vlm: vision model for text extraction.

.TP
.B \-\-ocr-dpi \fIDPI\fR
VLM engine only: Resolution in DPI for rasterizing page images.
Default: 200. Range: 72-600 recommended.

.TP
.B \-\-ocr-concurrency \fINUM\fR
VLM engine only: Number of concurrent page requests. Default: 8.

.TP
.B \-\-ocr-retries \fINUM\fR
VLM engine only: Retry attempts for failed requests. Default: 5.

.TP
.B \-\-ocr-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
VLM engine only: Request timeout in seconds. Default: 180 (3 minutes).

.TP
.B \-\-caffeinate
macOS only: Prevent system sleep during conversion. Useful for long
running batch conversions on laptops.

.TP
.B \-\-enhance \fIPATH\fR
Enhance an existing markdown file instead of converting a PDF.

.TP
.B \-\-chunks
Also produce chunked JSONL output. Each line is a JSON object with
text chunk and metadata. Required for search indexing.

.TP
.B \-\-chunk-size \fINUM\fR
Maximum tokens per chunk. Default: 1024.

.TP
.B \-\-chunker \fITYPE\fR
Chunking strategy: 'recursive' (default), 'semantic', 'sentence',
or 'hierarchical'.

.TP
.B \-\-index \fINAME\fR
Add the converted document to a named search index. Creates or appends
to the index database. Implies --chunks.

.TP
.B \-\-index-path \fIPATH\fR
Custom filesystem path for the search index database.

.TP
.B \-\-no-clean
Skip post-OCR cleanup passes. Produces raw OCR output without fixing
common issues like repeated headers/footers, page numbers, hyphenated
line breaks. Faster but less polished.

.TP
.B \-\-preserve-pages
Inject page markers into chunks so each chunk carries page_start and
page_end metadata. Required for page-level citations when using --index.

.TP
.B \-\-force
Force re-processing even if output file already exists.

.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show detailed progress information including per-page status, API
requests, and timing.

.TP
.B \-\-batch
Use Mistral Batch API for OCR (50% cost savings on directory runs).
Only available with mistral engine.

.TP
.B \-\-exclude \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude PDFs whose filename contains PATTERN. Can be repeated.

.SH BACKLOG COMMAND
The backlog command provides resumable batch PDF conversion:

.B pdfcancel backlog [OPTIONS] DIRECTORY

.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Output directory for all converted files. Default: each PDF converted
alongside its source.

.TP
.B \-\-exclude \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude PDFs matching pattern. Repeatable.

.TP
.B \-\-force
Force re-processing all PDFs even if already converted.

.TP
.B \-\-caffeinate
Prevent macOS system sleep during conversion.

The backlog command supports all VLM and mistral engine options described
above. It is checkpointed and signal-safe: Ctrl-C stops cleanly and
re-running resumes from where it left off.

 progress is tracked in <directory>/.pdfcancel_run.json and can be viewed
with:

.B pdfcancel status DIRECTORY

.SH SEARCH AND INDEXING
.pdfcancel supports creating searchable indexes of your document collection:

.TP
.B Create index
pdfcancel paper.pdf --index my_index
pdfcancel ./documents/ --index research

.TP
.B List indexes
pdfcancel indexes

.TP
.B Search
pdfcancel search my_index "query text"
pdfcancel search research "machine learning" --top-k 10
pdfcancel search cti "threat intelligence" --mode semantic --context

.TP
Search modes:
.IP "\fBhybrid\fR" 4
Combine keyword and semantic search (default)
.IP "\fBsemantic\fR" 4
Pure embedding-based search for meaning
.IP "\fBtext\fR" 4
Traditional keyword search only

.TP
Search options:
.IP "\fB\-k, \-\-top-k \fIN\fR" 4
Number of results (default: 10)
.IP "\fB\-\-context\fR" 4
Include neighboring chunks for more context
.IP "\fB\-\-index-path \fIPATH\fR" 4
Custom path for index database

.SH COMMAND REFERENCE
.TP
.B pdfcancel [PDF_FILE] [OPTIONS]
Convert a single PDF file to markdown.

.TP
.B pdfcancel backlog DIRECTORY [OPTIONS]
Resumable batch conversion of all PDFs in a directory.

.TP
.B pdfcancel status DIRECTORY
Show progress of a backlog run.

.TP
.B pdfcancel indexes
List all search indexes and their contents.

.TP
.B pdfcancel search INDEX_NAME "QUERY" [OPTIONS]
Search across indexed documents.

.TP
.B pdfcancel zotero [OPTIONS]
Zotero library integration (requires plugin).

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B MISTRAL_API_KEY
API key for Mistral's OCR service. Required when using mistral engine.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_API_BASE
Default API base URL for vlm engine. Override with --api-base.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_API_KEY
API key for vlm endpoint. Override with --api-key.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_OCR_ENGINE
Default OCR engine: 'mistral' or 'vlm'. Override with --ocr-engine.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_OCR_MODEL
Default OCR model for mistral engine. Override with --model.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_VLM_MODEL
Default vision model for vlm engine. Override with --model.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_MULTIMODAL_MODEL
Default vision model for --full image descriptions.

.TP
.B MISTRAL_BASE_URL
Mistral-compatible server URL. Override with --mistral-url.

.TP
.B MISTRAL_CA_BUNDLE
CA bundle (PEM) for verifying self-signed certificates.
Override with --ca-bundle or --mistral-ca-bundle.

.TP
.B PDFCANCEL_CA_BUNDLE
Same as MISTRAL_CA_BUNDLE (preferred for vlm engine).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Basic conversion
pdfcancel document.pdf

.TP
.B Convert with custom output
pdfcancel document.pdf -o ./markdown/

.TP
.B Full multimodal (text + image descriptions)
pdfcancel report.pdf --full

.TP
.B Use local Ollama
pdfcancel paper.pdf --api-base http://localhost:11434

.TP
.B Use vlm engine with specific model
pdfcancel paper.pdf --ocr-engine vlm --model llava:13b

.TP
.B Batch convert directory
pdfcancel backlog ./papers/

.TP
.B Batch with resumable progress
pdfcancel backlog ./papers/ --ocr-engine vlm --api-base http://localhost:11434
# Ctrl-C to interrupt
pdfcancel backlog ./papers/  # Resumes from checkpoint

.TP
.B Check progress
pdfcancel status ./papers/

.TP
.B Create and search index
pdfcancel ./docs/ --index research
pdfcancel search research "climate change"

.TP
.B Extract images
pdfcancel report.pdf --images

.TP
.B Embed images in markdown
pdfcancel slides.pdf --images --embed-images

.TP
.B Plain text output
pdfcancel document.pdf --plaintext

.TP
.B High quality for complex PDFs
pdfcancel complex.pdf --ocr-dpi 300 --no-clean

.TP
.B Exclude certain files
pdfcancel backlog ./all/ --exclude draft --exclude temp

.TP
.B Verbose output for debugging
pdfcancel document.pdf --verbose

.TP
.B Custom endpoint with API key
pdfcancel paper.pdf --api-base https://custom.endpoint/v1 --api-key sk-...

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Errors occurred during conversion
.TP
.B 2
Conversion incomplete or interrupted

.SH NOTES
For best results with the mistral engine, ensure you have a valid
MISTRAL_API_KEY set in your environment.

For local inference with the vlm engine, you'll need a running
OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, vLLM, LiteLLM, etc.) and the
--api-base flag pointing to it.

The --full flag requires a vision-capable model. Not all OCR models
support image description.

